MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_1="            YOUTUBE API SETUP INSTRUCTIONS"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_2="1. Visit https://console.cloud.google.com/"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_3="   Create or select your Google Cloud project."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_4="2. Enable \"YouTube Data API v3\" in API Library:"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_5="   https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_6="3. Configure Google Auth Platform consent screen."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_7="   For an External app in Testing, add your account as test user."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_8="   Testing refresh tokens may expire after 7 days."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_9="4. Create OAuth Client ID of type \"Desktop app\":"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_10="   https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/clients"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_11="5. Download its JSON credentials file."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_12="6. Back in MediaPanel select \"Install client_secrets.json\"."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_13="7. Select \"Authorize YouTube account\" to open your browser."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_14="8. Check token, then test API connection (read-only)."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_15="Notes:"
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_16="- Never commit client_secrets.json or token.json to Git."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_17="- OAuth credentials belong to each user, not the .deb package."
MP_YT_SETUP_INSTRUCTION_18="- API readiness requires an actual authorization / API check."
